{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>And you shall make a tzitz.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] translated it ʿaṭsaba. It is placed on the mitre and is not in the form of a crown, for it is on the forehead alone. For according to the plain sense, the migbaʿot are not in the form of a mitre, for the migbaʿot are like those that men in these lands place on the head to cover the head, and they are high. The mitre is a thin, long garment wrapped around the head alone; it somewhat resembles the mitre that women in these regions wear on their heads. For in the land of Ishmael and in Sepharad and Africa and Egypt, and in Babylonia and Baghdad, the mitre is on the heads of distinguished men, and not on the head of a woman. And the great officers make a golden tzitz upon the mitre at the place of the forehead. I have already mentioned to you that the custom of the land of Israel and their ornaments is not like the custom of these lands. Our master Solomon [Rashi] needed to emend the verses with three threads of tekhelet, but according to the plain sense there is no need except for a single cord to hold the tzitz on the face of the mitre that is on the forehead."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:38:54.045960672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}